  "notes": "Cash-basis county; only governmental funds, no business-type funds (business_type null). Attempt 2 (targeted re-check): balance sheet now taken from the Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p3, Total Governmental Funds column, fund balance by classification: restricted, committed, assigned, unassigned), since its totals (9,539,698) equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1). Investments 8,927,719 are included in total assets and in ending cash/fund balance roll-forward (the cash basis fund balance 9,539,698 includes investments), so beginning/ending_cash are total cash basis fund balances. Receipts and disbursements from Total Governmental Funds column p4. 'Taxes' is a single combined line with no breakdown anywhere (p2 general receipts also 'Taxes'), kept as taxes (unlabeled). Intergovernmental has no homestead/pro-rate breakdown in the report, kept whole. Transfers in/out 1,723,885 each (p4); cross-checked between funds: General out 1,704,677 = Road 1,700,000 + Development 4,677; 911 Wireless out 18,875 = General in; 911 EM out 333 = 911 Wireless in; none hidden in spending. Detail: General Fund budget schedule p5 used (only schedule for General Fund); Road, Buyback, Inheritance Tax budget schedules p6-7 give receipt lines but only total disbursements; nonmajor funds recorded from the combining Total Nonmajor column (p15) since there are more than 6 nonmajor funds (budget schedules pp8-11 give only total receipts/disbursements per fund and are not duplicated). Budget_final shown only where a budget schedule is the source. Public Health and zero lines omitted. Read pages 1-15 of 15"
